      "message": "FWIW: 32-bit x86 ART doesn\u0027t link because asm_support_x86.S\u0027s SETUP_GOT_NOSAVE is calling __x86.get_pc_thunk.bx. __x86.get_pc_thunk.* are compiler-generated functions that GCC emits into any object file that needs one. Clang doesn\u0027t emit these helper functions. Removing the last bit of GCC-compiled code (libatomic.a) may have broken it.\n\nA similar problem came up in Bionic -- I added a couple of thunks manually:\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/bionic/+/1289855/\n",
